#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f4.rst:5
#: be9778a0b2cf418abd1ceee6d1e007d4
msgid "SLCAN Access on F4 based Autopilots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f4.rst:7
#: abe9eeef519148e49f02d1ee0acbe056
msgid "Enabling SLCAN allows the autopilot to connect to CANBUS through USB on PC. It allows viewing, configuration and software updates of devices connected to the CANBUS. There are two different applications for using SLCAN to modify DroneCAN device parameter: DroneCAN GUI or Mission Planner. But first, the SLCAN interface must be enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f4.rst:11
#: f3c89b40f90643e589514ec66b4a2c7c
msgid "SLCAN access via COM port is disabled when armed to lower cpu load. Use SLCAN via MAVLink instead. MAVLink access is generally preferred in any case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f4.rst:14
#: c01c5221bb644e21b6d2735d995980e0
msgid "Enabling SLCAN"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f4.rst:16
#: a349412ac6e041428e2b6233b50df7f0
msgid "Connect the autopilot to Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f4.rst:18
#: 44e1799a42c5400ab7d6c62a3004f939
msgid "Set :ref:`CAN_SLCAN_CPORT<CAN_SLCAN_CPORT>` = 1, if not already set, or =2 if its desired to examine the second CAN bus, if the autopilot provides it, and reboot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f4.rst:22
#: 7d4053514d4a4b9cab7b468345325645
msgid "Connect normally to Mission Planner and navigate to Initial Setup->Optional Hardware->UAVCAN(DroneCAN). Click on SLCan Mode CAN1, and any attached DroneCAN nodes using Driver 1 will appear and firmware updates or parameter changes of the node are now available. To return to normal Mission Planner operation, leave this tab for 2 seconds and reconnect to Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f4.rst:28
#: d32de6d731614b8b98edd50d161c0806
msgid "Making Changes to DroneCAN Devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f4.rst:30
#: 4bfb2ab9261c43c28d805f3ce7531405
msgid "Once SLCAN has been enabled, you can use :ref:`Mission Planner <planner:dronecan-uavcan-slcan>`  to make changes immediately to device parameters or firmware update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f4.rst:32
#: 6fca3bdd5881427dbbdefe9b030bef4d
msgid ":ref:`DroneCAN GUI tool <common-uavcan-gui>` can also be used, but requires a slightly different setup:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f4.rst:35
#: a5bb615d6b084aa9bba5de756bb45a17
msgid "Enabling Use of DroneCAN GUI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f4.rst:37
#: b895ca358fff4ad4819fde7f447c89d7
msgid "Connect the flight autopilot to Mission Planner. Set the parameter :ref:`CAN_SLCAN_CPORT<CAN_SLCAN_CPORT>` = 1 , if not already set, and reboot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f4.rst:39
#: 102a2699cdf44754acec2904fb5007a4
msgid "Reconnect Mission Planner and set :ref:`CAN_SLCAN_SERNUM<CAN_SLCAN_SERNUM>` = 0. This will direct the output to the autopilot's SERIAL0 port which is normally the autopilot USB connection. Be sure that the :ref:`CAN_SLCAN_TIMOUT<CAN_SLCAN_TIMOUT>` parameter is 0 to prevent timeouts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f4.rst:43
#: a36f56df1449484b97e56c6f589cfd84
msgid "Do not reboot, and click SLCAN Mode CAN1 in the Initial Setup->Optional Hardware->UAVCAN(DroneCAN). Now open the :ref:`DroneCAN GUI tool<common-uavcan-gui>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f4.rst:45
#: 25f8cf7dde534b6ea6ee999365e8d878
msgid "In this mode, you can also use Mission Planner's DroneCAN page to make changes, but it will not connect normally as a MAVLink Ground Station. To re-connect Mission Planner, you will need to reboot the autopilot."
msgstr ""
